// THE VOTE TICKET. What voting hands out, and what you either sell or redeem - see
// configs/vote.constant for the model and why it is an item rather than a number.
//
// THE MODEL IS THE 377 TICKET, RECOLOURED. obj_paramayaticket is already shared by three tickets in
// this cache (the Paramaya ticket, the archery ticket and the Agility Arena ticket), all of them
// sage green and parchment, so a fourth one in the same colours would be unreadable in an
// inventory. The three face colours were read off models/obj/obj_paramayaticket.ob2 with
// tools/models/ob2palette.py - recol1s/2s/3s are its own three, not guesses - and they go to blue,
// near-white and deep blue. Nothing is imported and no art is touched: this is data.
//
// STACKABLE AND TRADEABLE, both on purpose. Stackable because a voter accumulates these and they
// must not eat the inventory; tradeable because selling them instead of redeeming them is half the
// model.
//
// cost=0 AND param=shop_will_not_buy. Five of this build's shops are allstock=yes and will buy any
// tradeable item at whatever cost= says, which would make voting a gp faucet at a fixed rate and
// take the price away from the players. The param refuses the sale outright (shop/scripts/shop.rs2,
// ~can_sell_obj); cost=0 is belt-and-braces so that if the param is ever lost the faucet is worth
// nothing rather than something.

[vote_ticket]
name=Vote ticket
desc=Redeem it for a vote point, or sell it to somebody who will.
model=obj_paramayaticket
// From ob2palette.py on obj_paramayaticket.ob2: three faces each of hsl16 16714, 7403 and 3532.
recol1s=19150
recol1d=10780
recol2s=31638
recol2d=29663
recol3s=25133
recol3d=6484
2dxof=6
2dyof=-2
2dzoom=830
2dyan=132
2dxan=320
stackable=yes
weight=0g
cost=0
iop1=Redeem
param=shop_will_not_buy,yes
